  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Diagonal commutes with base change",
  "statement": "For $X_\\lambda\\to S_\\lambda$ and $S\\to S_\\lambda$, the base change of\n$\\Delta_{X_\\lambda/S_\\lambda}$ is canonically identified with\n$\\Delta_{X_\\lambda\\times_{S_\\lambda}S/S}$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-prop-nagata-sketch-approximation/lemma-nagata-diagonal-base-change.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-diagonal-base-change, order 327"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Base change the defining fibre square of the diagonal. Associativity of\nfibre products identifies the result with the map sending a point to its\npair with itself, which is the diagonal of the base-changed morphism.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
